503 and deferred there; filed here rather than dropped.\n\n1. STALE DIVERGENCE. A declared divergence whose two surfaces have since CONVERGED must fail, so the\n   now-pointless declaration gets removed rather than lingering as a permanent waiver. The path\n   exists in _check_divergences but nothing exercises it.\n2. merge_declarations carry-forward. The commit s central safety claim is that --update carries\n   existing reasons forward and writes an EMPTY-reason stub for a newly-diverging tool, so it can\n   never launder a real divergence into silence. That behaviour is asserted nowhere.\n3. _check_normalization. Neither a schema_version change nor a change to\n   normalization.library_only_params between live and manifest is covered, so the category-level\n   rule that keeps 35 tools quiet could drift unnoticed.\n\nEach is a pure-function case against the already-injectable evaluate(live, manifest), so no new\nharness is needed. See scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py and tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8d66-52ad-b66c-485a","ticket_type":"task","title":"Cover the parity gate's untested evaluate paths","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f9946bb5-9b01-4736-976d-d8b0fdb6bb35","ab835595-36c9-44fe-a43c-1f93c25f75cb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788336565942799001,"uuid":"e023371c-ac3e-40cf-af32-de97e1a96a7b"}